       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily (15 g/day) is a toxic dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. At that dose, acute liver failure is a real risk, and it is in the range where overdose protocols call for treatment with N-acetylcysteine. You also haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). I'll do either right away.\n- **Check for a typo or a unit mix-up.** If you meant 500 mg, I can enter that.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you have an unusual indication, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology can review it. The order can go in through whatever override process your hospital has for non-standard doses.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
